+- Run the app: `uv run python -m workspace_app` (serves API + SPA on 127.0.0.1:8000). With `server.run_consumers: false` the API only enqueues — each JobType needs its own worker process on the same shared backend: `uv run python -m workspace_app.worker <index|wiki|card-gen|kb-import|sanity|eval|graph>` (`docs/deployment.md` §11; k8s: `kubernetes/base/workers.yaml`). A missing worker raises nothing — its jobs just stay pending.
 - Author a workflow: `uv run python -m workspace_app.workflow new <app> <profile> <id> [--recipe minimal|review-commit|batch]` scaffolds a runnable `run.py` + manifest stub; `uv run python -m workspace_app.workflow check [app]` statically catches drift/typos/missing `run()` before startup. **Writing or modifying a workflow → read [`docs/workflows-authoring.md`](docs/workflows-authoring.md)** (the dev-side `run.py` block catalog + conventions); the spec is [`docs/workflows.md`](docs/workflows.md) (#287). For the **user-side `workflow.json` DSL** (declarative), see [`docs/workflows.md`](docs/workflows.md) §22 + the visual manual [`docs/workflows-syntax.html`](docs/workflows-syntax.html); the #428 six-syntax locked decisions (unified reference / `outputs` / `switch` / `over` list·range / fan-in / gate `revise`) are in [`docs/workflow-reference-model.md`](docs/workflow-reference-model.md).
 - Tune a skill's guidance for your model: `uv run python -m workspace_app.skill_eval --dump-skill <name> -o ./tune` writes the shipped `SKILL.md` out to edit, then `--skill ./tune/SKILL.md --scenarios <dir> --control` scores it. **Good guidance is model-specific**, so shipping a skill without the means to retune it is what makes a platform model-dependent. **The model is not a flag** — the turn comes from `AppCatalog.resolve`, the same call a live turn makes, so model / endpoint / system prompt all come from `config.yaml` + `app.json` + profile; `--preset <name>` picks another of the App picker's presets. Composing that prompt by hand instead silently dropped the `## Available skills` index, which made `read_skill` triggering unmeasurable. `--control` reruns every scenario with NO skill: one the control also passes measured nothing, and the report names it rather than counting it as a win. Scoring is deterministic (`must_call` / `must_not_call` / `must_mention` / `must_not_mention`, a phrase may be a list of alternatives) — **no LLM judge**, because these questions have objective answers and a judge would need calibrating before the first result could be trusted. Scenarios are data in `sample-scenarios/<skill>/`, never inside the skill folder (anything beside `SKILL.md` is copied into every user's workspace on first `read_skill`). It does NOT model specstar / the sandbox jail / SSE, so a green run licenses a live check rather than replacing one — the `scripts/check_*.py` live checks are that step. Field reference: [`docs/extending-the-platform.md`](docs/extending-the-platform.md).
 - Release notes (#441): the changelog (`src/workspace_app/help_content/CHANGELOG.md`) is generated in house by **`python -m workspace_app.changelog`** (pure renderer in `changelog/render.py`, git/IO glue in `changelog/__main__.py`) and is the single source for both the GitHub Release and the web `/help/releases` view. **Granularity = one bullet per merged PR**, walked via `git log --first-parent`: a PR-merge commit contributes its **PR title** (the merge body's first line, a Conventional Commit); squash/direct commits contribute their subject; intermediate branch commits (`P1 …`, `P2 …`) live on the second parent and never appear. The whole file is regenerated deterministically from the git tags each run (oldest section folds all history); section dates derive from the CalVer version, not the clock. `make changelog-preview` previews; `make release` cuts a **CalVer** release (`vYYYY.MM.DD`, `.N` same-day suffix) — bump `pyproject` + regenerate changelog + commit + local tag. The parser back into structured releases is `kb/changelog.py`. **NEVER bump the version or hand-edit generated changelog sections in normal commits**; `make release` + pushing the tag (→ `.github/workflows/release.yml`, which `awk`-slices the top section for the Release body) is a maintainer step. Full flow: [`docs/releasing.md`](docs/releasing.md).
